        public static string TutBasicControlsStepOverlayElectricity = "This overlay shows device connections and assists in addressing issues with the power grid. It provides data on electricity production and consumption, any deficit, battery conditions, and also lists devices that are disconnected or switched off, among other useful details.";
        public static string TutBasicControlsStepOverlayAtmoo2 = "This visual overlay shows oxygen levels, making it useful for detecting leaks and areas unfit for living.";
        public static string TutBasicControlsStepOverlayAtmotemp = "This visual overlay displays temperature levels and helps to quickly identify any hot zones that could appear if industrial equipment is running in enclosed space without cooling or ventilation.";
        public static string TutBasicControlsStepOverlayAtmoo2res = "Airtightness measures how well something keeps oxygen contained within an area. This visual overlay helps spot open vents and damaged walls since they're not as airtight.";
        public static string TutBasicControlsStepOverlayAtmotempres = "Insulation represents the resistance to temperature exchange with the environment. Even if walls are fully airtight and don't let oxygen through, they can't fully block heat transfer. Heat will slowly move to surrounding areas, which is why maintaining comfortable temperatures takes more work than just keeping an area full of oxygen.";
        public static string TutBasicControlsStepOverlayPlan = "Along with a set of planning tools that include mirroring, circles, and lines, this overlay helps in designing the perfect ship. In scenarios where your ship is destroyed, the overlay will contain the original design, so you can choose to restore it to former glory or wipe everything out and make it your own.";
        public static string TutBasicControlsStepOverlayPath = "This overlay clarifies where and how your colonists and robots can move. Even when there appears to be a passable gap, the path might still be blocked. Remember, beings cannot move through diagonal passageways.";
        public static string TutBasicControlsStepOverlayAreas = "This overlay shows enclosed areas, room names (available once you unlock the Signs and Labeling research), and lists the devices in each room. It also reveals areas exposed to space and lets you toggle the outer hull display.<br><br>Incoming spacecraft can't land in enclosed areas, so ensure there are enough landing zones open to space. A landing area smaller than roughly 100 tiles might lead to issues.<br><br>Another important point: certain devices and all spacecraft need to be in areas open to space. If a device meant for outdoor use is enclosed, it won't work. Enclosing a shuttle may damage the hull when it tries to take off or land.";
        /// <summary>
        /// Version: 2023-08-16
        /// </summary>
        public static string TutBasicControlsStepOverlayIslands = "This overlay reveals separate ship sections. Sections are individual islands of structure. Usually, having more than one means the ship won't fly, though tiny sections with less than roughly 30 tiles are ignored. You can use <b>Winch</b> or <b>Maneuvering Controller</b> to pull these sections together.<br><br>The overlay also lets you abandon any unwanted ship sections, including derelict ships you might come across during your adventure. You'll need to attach, disassemble, or abandon a derelict ship before flying away.<br><br>When near a space port, you can use this overlay to sell a section. This makes it possible to temporarily attach a derelict ship to your own, tow it to the nearest space port, detach it, and then sell it.";
        /// <summary>
        /// Version: 2023-08-16
        /// </summary>
        public static string TutBasicControlsStepFeedback = "If you encounter issues, discover a bug, or have a suggestion, you can submit your feedback directly from the game.";
