        public static string TutBodypartsStep1_1 = "All robotic and biological <b>Beings</b> possess various <b>Body Parts</b> and <b>Organs</b>. These components can add <b>Abilities</b> and <b>Needs</b>, and modify <b>Stats</b>.";
        /// <summary>
        /// {0} is replaced with skull icon, doesn&apos;t affect translation
        /// </summary>
        public static string TutBodypartsStep1_5_V1 = "The most important part of any robot is the <b>Core</b>, which contains the bot's identity, skills, memories, experiences, and traits. If this part is <b>Irreparably</b> damaged, the robot is considered {0} <b>Dead</b>.<br><br>For biological beings, this part is the <b>Brain</b>.";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep2Title = "Injuries and Wounds";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep3_1 = "Selecting a being will reveal any active or developing <b>Conditions</b>, including <b>Wounds</b> from physical injuries. It can help identify the <b>cause of death</b> as well.";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep3_2_V1 = "Some conditions, such as <b>Depression</b>, have mental effects, while others, like <b>Hypoxia</b>, can cause physical injuries that can lead to {0} <b>Death</b>.";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep3_3 = "Most conditions have an underlying <b>root cause</b>. Fixing the cause allows the condition to <b>recover</b> over time.<br><br>Example: <b>Depression</b> develops when the <b>Fun</b> stat remains low. Providing <b>Entertainment</b> facilities can increase <b>Fun</b> and gradually reduce <b>Depression</b>.";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep4_1 = "For biological beings, some wounds can be <b>Fatal</b>. However, if the <b>Brain</b> remains intact, it can be <b>transferred</b> into a different body.";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep4_2 = "Brains can even be swapped between <b>different species</b>. For example, transplanting the brain of a <b>Cat</b> into the body of a <b>Human</b> will result in a human with the identity of the cat, who will behave like one.";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep4_3 = "While you cannot install a <b>Brain</b> into a robot, and cannot replace the <b>Brain</b> with a robotic <b>Core</b> in a biological being, it is possible to perform a <b>Mind Transfer</b> using the <b>Replicator</b>.";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep4_4 = "Using a <b>Core</b> removed from a defeated <b>enemy</b> will <b>resurrect</b> the enemy, but with the help of a <b>Replicator</b>, you can <b>overwrite</b> the enemy's <b>identity</b> with one from a <b>friendly</b> colonist <b>Brain</b>.<br><br>This is a great way to expand your robotic workforce by giving a second life to your fallen biological colonists.";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep5Title = "Body Part Operations";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep5_3 = "To use the <b>Replicator</b>, both the <b>Core</b> and the <b>Brain</b> must first be removed from the bodies.";
        public static string TutBodypartsStep5_6 = "Biological organs can be <b>harvested</b> at the <b>Surgery Hub</b>.";
        /// <summary>
        /// Version: 2024-11-19
        /// </summary>
        public static string ObjectsDevicesMemorymoduleminiDesc_V1 = "{0} Exabytes of Memory (RAM). Used alongside a GPU for mining cryptocurrencies.";
        public static string CombatGoalAttackTurret = "Attack Turret";
        public static string CombatObjectiveSurvive = "Survive";
        public static string NounLeader = "Leader";
        public static string NounFollower = "Follower";
        public static string NounSquadRole = "Squad Role";
        public static string TutCombatTitle = "Combat Tactics";
        public static string TutCombatDesc = "This tutorial will teach you how to <b>defend your ship</b> against <b>Raids</b> and <b>Hostile Creatures</b>.";
        public static string TutCombatStep1Title = "Security Measures";
        public static string TutCombatStep1_1 = "Using available <b>security measures</b> is the first and one of the most important steps to <b>achieving victory</b> in any battle.";
        public static string TutCombatStep1_1_2 = "<b>Repair Stations</b> are essential for <b>repairing</b> your <b>damaged robotic workers</b>.";
        public static string TutCombatStep1_2 = "<b>Doors</b> can be <b>Locked</b> to block access. With <b>Door Permissions</b> research, even <b>Unlocked</b> doors will keep <b>enemies</b> out unless configured otherwise.<br><br><b>Door Permissions</b> can also be set to <b>deny access</b> to certain <b>friendly beings</b>.";
        public static string TutCombatStep1_2_2 = "<b>Bot Docks</b> can be assigned to specific <b>robotic workers</b>. The workers will <b>idle</b> and <b>recharge</b> in their docks when they have no ongoing tasks.<br><br>Deploying <b>Bot Docks</b> in <b>strategic locations</b> can ensure the fastest response to incoming <b>raids</b>.";
        public static string TutCombatStep1_3 = "An <b>Emergency Siren</b> can hail your <b>biological colonists</b> to a safe zone. It can be triggered either <b>automatically</b> or <b>manually</b>.<br><br>Colonists won't be happy when sirens are blaring, so don't forget to turn them <b>off</b> when it's <b>safe</b>.";
        public static string TutCombatStep1_4 = "Deploy <b>Mini Turrets</b> in strategic positions to protect <b>important areas</b> and <b>entry points</b>.<br><br>To avoid compromising <b>Hull Integrity</b>, these turrets aren't especially powerful, but they remain highly effective.";
        public static string TutCombatStep1_5 = "<b>Fluid Cannons</b> can be fueled with almost any type of <b>liquid</b>. When fueled with <b>Water</b>, they not only deal <b>light damage</b> to <b>enemies</b> but also <b>extinguish fires</b>.<br><br>When fueled with <b>Petroleum</b> or <b>Oil</b>, the <b>Fluid Cannon</b> fires <b>incendiary bullets</b> that <b>ignite fires</b> on impact. It is safer to use outdoors in areas without <b>Oxygen</b>.";
        public static string TutCombatStep1_6 = "<b>Trap Floors</b> will impale <b>grounded enemies</b> as they pass over them.";
        public static string TutCombatStep1_7 = "Normally, you open <b>Floor Vents</b> to cool an area, but if a <b>grounded enemy</b> is standing over one, they will be <b>vented into space</b>.";
        public static string TutCombatStep1_9 = "This is the <b>Tractor Beam Target</b>. It's best to deploy it <b>outside</b>, far from the <b>living quarters</b>.";
        public static string TutCombatStep2Title = "Combat Reactions";
        public static string TutCombatStep4Title = "Controlling Multiple Units";
